      "title": "QM9",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "QM9",
        "“Small” scale dataset with ~134,000 stable organic molecules (up to 9 heavy atoms)",
        "and 19 computed quantum properties per molecule.",
        "• Widely used to train and benchmark ML models on molecular property prediction.",
        "• All target properties are invariant under rotations and translations of the molecule."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "505e6d959057e4a4510bdc145b641d99bbdf2003b53983bd2ffb5d89f2096fc9",
        "564367ce42360449417f4ab5abaa5b8d6c52baaec7e525ccd17c09eff6cc9112"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "slide": 5,
      "pptx_slide": 5,
      "title": "MD17, rMD17",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "MD17, rMD17",
        "• A collection of thousands of snapshots from ab initio molecular",
        "dynamics simulations for 10 small organic molecules.",
        "• e.g. benzene, aspirin.",
        "• Each snapshot provides the molecule’s 3D atomic positions,",
        "its total potential energy, and the force vector on each atom.",
        "• rMD17 (revised MD17) took 100,000 snapshots from the original",
        "MD17 dataset and recalculates the energies and forces."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "51977b6625ca8659b254f2c42b92573e42a435942d87901c9294490d605a453a",
