      "pptx_slide": 8,
      "title": "Open Catalyst (OC20, OC22)",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "Open Catalyst (OC20, OC22)",
        "• A large-scale dataset of molecular adsorption",
        "on catalyst surfaces, released by Meta.",
        "• Adsorbate means an atom or molecule attached to a",
        "catalyst surface – an important scenario for",
        "chemical reactions in energy applications.",
        "• It contains 1,281,040 DFT “relaxation” trajectories",
        "– simulations of molecules (adsorbates) binding to",
        "surfaces – totaling ~264 million individual",
        "energy/force calculations.",
        "• S2EF (Structure to Energy & Forces – given a",
        "structure, predict its energy and forces) and IS2RE",
        "(Initial Structure to Relaxed Energy – predict the",
        "final energy from the initial configuration)."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "d1dc63ff096f17058b8ebebf71fb236add6a8428047e8d3bf0ab03379b10aa08",
