    {
      "slide": 14,
      "pptx_slide": 14,
      "title": "MDR Phonon Benchmark",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "MDR Phonon Benchmark",
        "• A phonon is like a quantized sound wave in a solid that",
        "describes a way the atoms in the material can vibrate.",
        "• Low-frequency phonons correspond to atoms oscillating gently,",
        "while high-frequency phonons are fast vibrations.",
        "• Phonon properties determine things like thermal conductivity",
        "and stability of a material.",
        "• This benchmark uses a dataset of ~10,000 materials with",
        "computed phonon spectra from the",
        "Materials Data Repository (MDR)."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "7b4b5406acc1a52955d0ad44281abdf4f40fd341a15ab7ce5a4b39c709d9dcf3"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
